@startuml extract_text_flow
' v25.2 — reasoning models: how one reply becomes text (or a named failure).
' See docs/design-addendum-provider.md §L.
!include _style.puml
title ai::extractText — the reply contains more than the answer (v25.2)

start
:reply bytes from the wire
(ChatClient / LlmQuickAddClient);
if (parses as a JSON object?) then (no)
  #F7E9E8:error: "AI reply was not JSON";
  stop
endif
switch (dialect?)
case (Anthropic)
  :walk content[] to the
  **first text block**
  (v21.2 — never index [0]);
case (OpenAI)
  :text = message.content;
  if (empty after scrub?) then (yes)
    #EDF4F1:fall back to message.reasoning,
    then reasoning_content
    <i>(recover a discarded answer —</i>
    <i>never concatenate onto one)</i>;
  else (no — content beats reasoning)
  endif
endswitch
:**strippedOfThinking()** — both dialects
remove every ~<think>…~</think> span
an <b>unclosed</b> ~<think> drops to the end
<i>(half a deliberation must not leak)</i>;
if (anything left?) then (no)
  #F7E9E8:error: "AI reply had no text content"
  <i>(now only when the reply truly</i>
  <i>holds no answer)</i>;
  stop
endif
#EDF4F1:TextResult{ok, text}
-> nlp::llm fences / chat bubble;
stop

note right
  V72's bug class, both paths:
  Anthropic fixed it by **walking blocks** (v21.2);
  OpenAI needed a **scrub + fallback** (v25.2),
  because there the deliberation arrives
  <i>inside</i> the string, not beside it.
end note
@enduml
